{"id":94,"date":"2026-07-09T14:25:53","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T14:25:53","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/localhost:8181\/ductless-comfort-for-pittsburgh-rowhouses-from-lawrenceville-to-the-slopes\/"},"modified":"2026-07-14T19:43:53","modified_gmt":"2026-07-14T19:43:53","slug":"ductless-comfort-for-pittsburgh-rowhouses-from-lawrenceville-to-the-slopes","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/ductless-comfort-for-pittsburgh-rowhouses-from-lawrenceville-to-the-slopes\/","title":{"rendered":"Your Pittsburgh Rowhouse Has a Front Door Two Floors Above the Yard"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover alignfull s-hero-offset\" style=\"min-height:500px;padding-top:6rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:3rem;aspect-ratio:unset;\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim-40 has-background-dim\"><\/span><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-1484\" alt=\"rowhouse - professional HVAC service photo\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-rowhouse-1-1024x683.png\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-rowhouse-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-rowhouse-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-rowhouse-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-rowhouse-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-cover-is-layout-15083543 wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-hero-offset__card has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-b267b866 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:3rem\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Rowhouses built for hillsides, not ducts<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A rowhouse built into a hillside has a front door on one floor and a back yard two floors down \u2014 and its comfort problems are just as vertical.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Schedule the Walkthrough<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"s-trust-bar\"><div class=\"s-trust__item\">15+ Years Serving PA<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Licensed &amp; Insured<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Same-Day Emergency<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Local to Your Area<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-stats is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">10-15\u00b0F<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Vertical temperature split in unzoned rowhouses<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">3<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Floors needing independent zone control<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">$400-600<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Annual savings from floor-by-floor zoning<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">1<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Penetration per indoor head required<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-pills s-pills--outline\">\n<li>No ductwork in 100-year-old framing<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Party walls are load-bearing masonry<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Stack effect pulls heat upward in winter<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Third floor bakes in summer alone<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Line-set routing must respect facades<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Condenser mounting on zero flat ground<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why ducts lose the argument<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Retrofitting central air into a Pittsburgh rowhouse means finding vertical paths for supply and return trunks through a house that has none. The party walls on both sides are structural masonry \u2014 off limits. The interior walls are plaster over wood lath, usually load-bearing along the stair.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Three stacked floors over a walk-out basement behave like a chimney: heated air migrates up and out through the top level while cold air is drawn in below. A single air handler in the basement, pushing through improvised ductwork, fights that vertical gradient from the worst possible position. Ductless sidesteps all of it.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Refrigerant lines are under an inch in diameter, they route through a single small penetration per head, and each head conditions the floor it sits on instead of relying on air pushed up from below.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b.jpg\" alt=\"boiler pipes heating system\" class=\"wp-image-186\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b-300x200.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;Pipes&quot; by twoshortplanks, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Rowhouse HVAC solutions by floor<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-feature-row is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1755\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ground Floor<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Larger capacity head handles front and rear exposures, entry infiltration, highest winter load.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1756\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Middle Floor<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Most protected space, insulated on both sides by neighbors&#039; heated homes. Modest mid-sized head.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg\" alt=\"hvac technician repair\" class=\"wp-image-188\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;AC Service&quot; by SuperTech HVAC Services, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Top Floor<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Roof load plus summer stack effect. Bedroom-sized head with independent setpoint control.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Per-floor load comparison<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-table s-table--modern has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Floor<\/th><th>Winter Heat Loss<\/th><th>Summer Gain<\/th><th>Typical Head Size<\/th><th>Independent Control<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>First (Front\/Rear)<\/td><td>High<\/td><td>Moderate<\/td><td>18,000\u201324,000 BTU<\/td><td>Separate thermostat<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Middle (Interior)<\/td><td>Low<\/td><td>Low<\/td><td>9,000\u201312,000 BTU<\/td><td>Separate thermostat<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Third (Roof + Stack)<\/td><td>Moderate<\/td><td>High<\/td><td>12,000\u201315,000 BTU<\/td><td>Separate thermostat<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text\" style=\"grid-template-columns:50% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1.png\" alt=\"minisplit - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1765\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Line-set routing on brick facades<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The refrigerant lines, condensate drain, and control wire between each indoor head and the outdoor unit have to travel down the outside of the building. On brick rowhouses that run is the most visible decision in the whole project. The default should be the rear elevation \u2014 the yard-facing wall almost nobody sees \u2014 with lines dropping in a straight vertical run inside painted line-hide channel.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Penetrations deserve equal care: drill through mortar joints, not brick faces, so the hole remains repairable if equipment is ever removed. Condensate has its own gravity problem on a slope. A head on the downhill side may drain to daylight; the uphill side sits below grade and needs a small condensate pump. Neither is a defect \u2014 both need to be in the plan before install week.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Six numbers to settle before drilling brick<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-indent has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Rowhouse ductless jobs go wrong in planning, not installation. These six measurements must appear in writing before any quote is final \u2014 if a proposal arrives without them, it was written for a generic house, not yours.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The six-point design audit<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-steps\">\n<li>Per-floor heat loss and gain, calculated from wall construction and window count<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Wall composition at each penetration \u2014 multi-wythe brick, veneer, or block \u2014 dictates drilling method<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Total line-set length per zone, checked against manufacturer limits that tall houses approach faster<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Electrical panel capacity and breaker availability for dedicated 240V circuit<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Condensate path for every head \u2014 gravity drain or pump \u2014 marked before pricing<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Outdoor unit placement sketched on actual elevation with snow depth and party-wall clearance<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Condenser mounting options for hillside lots<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-cards-3 is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Rear gravel pad<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Leveled composite base on graded yard. Best option when slope allows. Straight line-set run, minimal vibration transmission.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Wall-mounted bracket<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bolted into masonry with vibration isolators. Common in this city. Must be above walkways and snow drifts. Never hangs over neighbor&#039;s path.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Terraced deck mount<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Porch roof or addition roof with engineered stand. Requires structural review. Elevates unit above snow and roof drain lines.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Hillside neighborhoods: site-specific routing<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Allegheny County&#039;s river valleys built vertically because terrain gave them no choice. The pattern repeats from South Side Slopes to Polish Hill to Spring Hill to streets above the West End. Lawrenceville and Bloomfield add a flatter variant \u2014 long, deep rowhouses where the vertical problem is milder but the no-ductwork constraint is identical.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Historic district designations may require approval for equipment visible from the street, which is one more argument for rear-elevation line-set routing. The rivers themselves contribute muggy summer air: a ductless head running long, low-speed cooling cycles wrings moisture far better than window units slamming on and off \u2014 which is the upgrade most third-floor bedrooms in this city are actually waiting for.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Duquesne Light serves the entire grid and offers demand-response credits for homes with smart thermostats. Peoples Gas delivers through these narrow hillside streets and covers high-efficiency furnace installs. On South Side Slopes between 18th and 21st, condenser placement often requires wall brackets \u2014 yards slope too steeply for ground pads.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In Troy Hill along Lowrie Street, each brick rowhouse has a unique rear elevation \u2014 cookie-cutter plans fail because no two pathways are alike.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-diagnostic has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-b267b866 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:3rem\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Hillside rowhouse comfort diagnosis<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Top floor 10+ degrees warmer than basement level \u2014 vertical zoning needed<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Condensers on hillside grade shifting position \u2014 mounting pad or bracket required<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Line-set routing visible on front facade \u2014 aesthetic routing through rear preferred<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Party-wall side comfortable, exterior side cold \u2014 directional heat loss confirms insulation gaps<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Stairwell acts as chimney in winter \u2014 stack effect pulling heated air upward and out<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Rowhouse ductless questions we hear in Pittsburgh<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-accordion s-accordion--cards has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1583283a wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>One multi-zone condenser or separate outdoor units per floor?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Usually one multi-zone outdoor unit, because hillside lots rarely have room for two or three. Separate units win when floors have wildly different schedules \u2014 a rented ground floor, for instance \u2014 or when a single unit&#039;s minimum output exceeds the smallest head&#039;s needs. The load math decides it, not a default.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Will wall penetrations hurt the brick or the house&#039;s value?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A correctly sleeved three-inch hole through a mortar joint is a repairable, reversible modification \u2014 repointing restores the joint if equipment is removed. What damages masonry is careless drilling through brick faces and unsealed penetrations. The method is the whole difference.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Can ductless really carry a Pittsburgh January without the boiler?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cold-climate models hold strong output at five degrees and keep operating well below zero, covering nearly all local winter hours. Many owners keep an existing boiler as backup for deepest cold and resale flexibility. Houses with aging boilers often retire them entirely. Both designs are legitimate when sized honestly.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>How much does a three-zone rowhouse system cost installed?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Multi-zone systems range from $8,500 to $15,000 installed, depending on wall composition, line-set routing complexity, and condenser mounting method. Rear-elevation bracket mounts cost less than wall-drilled penetrations on masonry that requires specialized bits. Request an actual site walkthrough for accurate pricing.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-quote s-quote--mark has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>Hold a tissue at your stairwell. If it moves upward, stack effect is stealing your conditioned air in winter and pulling hot air into the top floor in summer.<\/p><cite>Pittsburgh HVAC diagnostic<\/cite><\/blockquote><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-overlap has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-10371125 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-overlap__img has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large alignwide\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1475\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-overlap__card has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-bfed0f9d wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:2.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:2.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Start with the walkthrough, not the brochure<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A rowhouse ductless design visit walks every floor, checks wall construction, sketches the line-set run on your actual rear elevation, and confirms the electrical panel can carry the load. You end up with a plan drawn for your house on your hill \u2014 a document any contractor&#039;s bid can be checked against. The six numbers above don&#039;t come from a generic form.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They come from measuring your walls, calculating your floor-by-floor loads, and solving the specific puzzle of where to mount a condenser when the ground won&#039;t cooperate. That walkthrough is the only way to separate a design from a brochure.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--dark-gradient s-band--spacious has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-cta--fullbleed has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Book the rowhouse walkthrough<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We&#039;ll measure, calculate, and sketch the six numbers above on your actual house. You&#039;ll get a design proposal drawn for your floor layout and your facade.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Schedule the Visit<\/a><\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is